        "m1": {
          "type": "phase",
          "settings": {
            "label": "1 Month",
            "title": "Inflammation markers.",
            "body": "<p>Multiple randomized controlled trials have demonstrated that quercetin supplementation significantly reduces circulating CRP — a primary biomarker of systemic inflammation. If you track labs, this is what to watch.</p>"
          }
        },
        "m3": {
          "type": "phase",
          "settings": {
            "label": "3–6 Months",
            "title": "Skin. Glucose. Cardiovascular.",
            "body": "<p>Resveratrol has been studied for improved insulin sensitivity. Antioxidant protection of skin cells accumulates. Cardiovascular markers — the ones your doctor watches — are the territory you're working in now.</p>"
          }
        },
        "y1": {
          "type": "phase",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Years",
            "title": "Healthspan, compounding.",
            "body": "<p>Lifespan isn't built <em>then</em> — when things start to slow, when the labs shift, when you finally feel it. It's built and managed <em>now</em>. Sirtuin activation. Slower biological aging. The quiet, compounding work of staying ahead of it.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
